<section id="faqs"><h2>Frequently asked: Demolition &amp; Deconstruction in Vancouver</h2><h3>What does house demolition cost in Vancouver in 2026?</h3><p>$28,000 to $48,000 for a standard pre-war SFH including deconstruction, hazmat, disposal, and salvage credit.</p>
<h3>Whats the difference between demolition and deconstruction?</h3><p>Demolition smashes and disposes. Deconstruction dismantles in reverse — required by City of Vancouver bylaw for homes built before 1950, with 75 percent material diversion mandatory.</p>
<h3>How long does the process take?</h3><p>Deconstruction: 14 to 21 working days. Standard demo: 3 to 5 days. Hazmat abatement adds 5 to 10 days.</p>
<h3>Asbestos testing — do I need it?</h3><p>Yes — WorkSafeBC mandates pre-demo hazmat survey for any structure built before 1990. Lab turnaround 5 to 10 business days.</p>
<h3>Why demolition.io exclusive territory?</h3><p>One verified deconstruction contractor per metro. Generals stop losing permits at City Hall and start passing inspection on the first walk-through.</p>
